what has been almost a month now since  governor sisal acts directive to close  non-essential business here in Nevada  and Las Vegas mayor Carolyn Goodman is  now speaking out urging the governor to  reopen our economy soon  Hector Mejia is live on the strip with  the mayor's comments good morning to you  Hector good morning Alex shops and  resorts are closed here we have the  encore right behind us and the mayor  says it's her belief that the corona  virus is not going away anytime soon and  therefore these places should reopen  mayor Carolyn Goodman made remarks  during yesterday's City Council meeting  on March 17th  governor steve says elect issued a  directive closing all non-essential  businesses including casinos to slow the  spread of corona virus he joined several  other governor's in that decision our  tourism industry has been on hold since  then while Goodman sent her condolences  to families who have lost loved ones to  coated 19 she also emphasized those  debts quote caused the entire state to  shut down from my perspective I am  asking open the city open Clark County  open the state for heaven's sakes for  being closed is killing us already and  killing Las Vegas our industry our  Convention and tourism business that we  have all worked so hard to build the  longer we wait to do this the more  impossible it will become to recover  she said 900,000 Nevadans are out of  work so far almost 300,000 have filed  for unemployment according to the  governor and we reached out to his  office a couple of times yesterday and  so far we have not received a response  back reporting live this morning Hector  Mejia 8 News now
 

